   - The base cases handle edge conditions (n ≤ 1, n == 2) and early termination if a divisor is found.

2. **Array Reversal Function (`reverseArray`)**:
   - This function reverses the array by recursively swapping elements from the start and end indices moving towards the center.
   - The base case stops the recursion when the start index is greater than or equal to the end index.
   - Each recursive call swaps the elements and moves the indices inward.

